{"authored" [{"question" "q-77709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/fa8ce497e80e941730cebb8528b09725930fcb31c839ac0020ce7cf9f0a39b58.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is shown above. Which of the following is $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}},$ the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "13a1dc8b64deb7ca6765d314afb77313665a825c4e3c70c62b2258bca128e50d" "basis" 1013 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77709" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(-3,6)$ and ${B}^{′}(5,-3),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/26d4f8e966818e27a0858da0aa8757cf71ebbd1ef0e0544a2b8a126810252def.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "13a1dc8b64deb7ca67