4afb77313665a825c4e3c70c62b2258bca128e50d" "basis" 1013 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-77709" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/26d4f8e966818e27a0858da0aa8757cf71ebbd1ef0e0544a2b8a126810252def.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "13a1dc8b64deb7ca6765d314afb77313665a825c4e3c70c62b2258bca128e50d" "basis" 1013 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-159801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/d9ec98b03009d1023668aa12de88ed5515f0ea6df058d1b5d17804bf42082c5c.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "13a1dc8b64deb7ca6765d314afb77313665a825c4e3c70c62b2258bca128e50d" "basis" 1013 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-159801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(6,4),(1,-6),(-3,2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4c43c4c793924d4fde32b59c93b7a19be0109a389b126665868396b4c06d721e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "13a1dc8b64deb7ca6765d314afb77313665a825c4e3c70c62b2258bca128e50d" "basis" 1013 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-159801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "05374865d4d6a8be836ddaec0b406b0587de6ded509e6ed871d1bca1b6c8fa4f" "basis" 1013 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-159801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/state.json" "file_sha256" "13a1dc8b64deb7ca6765d314afb77313665a825c4e3c70c62b2258bca128e50d" "basis" 1013 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-159801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course