3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-281567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $GHI$ has vertices at $G(5,5),\\,H(-1,-4),$ and $I(3,5).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding vertices of  $△{G}^{′}{H}^{′}{I}^{′}$, the image of $△GHI$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${G}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$),\\,$  $\\,{H}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$),\\,$ $\\,{I}^{′}($ \n{{field-5}}, \n{{field-6}}\n$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-281567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $△GHI$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $GHI:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 15 & -17 \\\\ 25 & -14 & 21\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{G}^{′}{H}^{′}{I}^{′}$ are ${G}^{′}(-15,25),$\n${H}^{′}(15,-14),$ ${I}^{′}(-17,21).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-281567" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refere