e" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-12033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-2,1),(3,3),$ and $(5,-2).$ Which of the following are coordinates of a vertex of ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(5,-2)$\n- $(-2,-5)$\n- $(3,12)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-12033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 12 & 13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-2,-5),(3,12),(5,13).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-12033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1e06934bfab72d672f84bb3eaf4fa074d8173d62241a1d7d47788ab5c7c79745"} {"question" "q-12033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-12033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-12033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-159801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/d9ec98b03009d1023668aa12de88ed5515f0ea6df058d1b5d17804bf42082c5c.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-159801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(6,4),(1,-6),(-3,2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/4c43c4c793924d4fde32b59c93b7a19be0109a389b126665868396b4c06d721e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-159801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1e06934bfab72d672f84bb3eaf4fa074d8173d62241a1d7d47788ab5c7c79745"} {"question" "q-159801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-159801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refer