under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(21,0)$\n- $(3,0)$\n- $(-21,0)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-8125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-21,0),(21,0),(0,3).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-8125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1e06934bfab72d672f84bb3eaf4fa074d8173d62241a1d7d47788ab5c7c79745"} {"question" "q-8125" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-8125" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-8125" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-8097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,1),(2,3),$ and $(5,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of a vertex of ${S}^{′}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(4,-1)$\n- $(17,-3)$\n- $(10,-1)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-8097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 17 & 10 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(4,-1),(17,-3),(10,-1).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-8097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1e06934bfab72d672f84bb3eaf4fa074d8173d62241a1d7d47788ab5c7c79745"} {"question" "q-8097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-8097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "q-8097" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/state.json" "file_sha256" "9248904f1840495dab3fe2b10b0995e87ff2189a34c288482791aa6d582f1092"} {"question" "e-6682" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/73f0065d4d4768a2c3432559702c2db28fefd050194a5bcdfe44ac3e0b736c82.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{AB}$ is shown below. Find $\\overline{A'B'},$ the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/2e22400d15abc81150d6d18de591549e81a46bd16ab9e95f10f86bae2125b490.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/example-6682.json" "file_sha256" "0719414a1d2b4fe6e92c4247ba80b1ef5f14e31f71be0566f446f9142e8464e0"} {"question" "e-6682" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overline{AB}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/fe82a0c8616e43c9d8db0b2892a145fcabf4cfa17bd3d4e033a1349cd25921ee.png)\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are $A'(1,3)$ and $B'(1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/472f8e712f7d695d5ab3593dafbcc0309feb1a6ac80e9e29c4893dc651d20cf7.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/example-6682.json" "file_sha256" "0719414a1d2b4fe6e92c4247ba80b1ef5f14e31f71be0566f446f9142e8464e0"} {"question" "e-5447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/10c3819b661a1831f747c949089a9133b4d0df7b07a66efe588c12bab469136e.png)\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown below. Find $\\triangle A'B'C',$ the image of $\\triangle ABC$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/4986bd2dab6b455c0d5e41909377c433d761bf7270364d3e2596e6db7f23981b.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/example-5447.json" "file_sha256" "a06af081b133b97bc3fc99e9ba9496d104bdcefe813785646e2271f609b33b3a"} {"question" "e-5447" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $\\triangle ABC\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/0cd1d198e714f41437302bdf21c17979409a533d3055b5b4dc519855d6fc8efb.png)\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $\\triangle A'B'C'$ are $(-3,-4), (0,0), (1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/assets/e8a14ffbaab4597a2a4a7c9a6bad61dabbc4970fc22c3ed2eb28b2594a670938.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14056071/example-5447.json" "file_sha256" "a06af081b133b97bc3fc99e9ba9496d104bdcefe813785646e2271f609b33b3a"}] "usage" {"q-8097" [] "q-77709" [] "q-159801" [] "e-6682" [] "e-5447" []} "basis" 1825 "retractions" [[17592186283518 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/fa8ce497e80e941730cebb8528b09725930fcb31c839ac0020ce7cf9f0a39b58.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is shown above. Which of the following is $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}},$ the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$"] [17592186283518 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(-3,6)$ and ${B}^{′}(5,-3),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/26d4f8e966818e27a0858da0aa8757cf71ebbd1ef0e0544a2b8a126810252def.png)"] [17592186283466 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/d9ec98b03009d1023668aa12de88ed5515f0ea6df058d1b5d17804bf42082c5c.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$"] [17592186283466 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(6,4),(1,-6),(-3,2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4c43c4c793924d4fde32b59c93b7a19be0109a389b126665868396b4c06d721e.png)"] [17592186088332 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1, 1), (2, 3)$, and $(5, 1)$. Which of the following are coordinates of a vertex of $S^{′}$, the image of $S$ under the action of $T$?\n\n1. $(4,-1)$\n2. $(17,-3)$\n3. $(10,-1)$"] [17592186087547 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe line segment $\\overline{AB}$ is shown below. Find $\\overline{A'B'},$ the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/2e22400d15abc81150d6d18de591549e81a46bd16ab9e95f10f86bae2125b490.png)"] [17592186087547 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $\\overline{AB}$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overline{AB}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are $A'(1,3)$ and $B'(1,-2),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/472f8e712f7d695d5ab3593dafbcc0309feb1a6ac80e9e29c4893dc651d20cf7.png)"] [17592186087501 :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is shown below. Find $\\triangle A'B'C',$ the image of $\\triangle ABC$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990291/assets/4986bd2dab6b455c0d5e41909377c433d761bf7270364d3e2596e6db7f23981b.png)"] [17592186087501 :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $\\triangle ABC\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $\\triangle A'B'C'$ are $(-3,-4), 